<Docs
	page="recipes/cxx"
	title="C++"
	lede="sqlite3, libpq, and libpqxx work out of the box, the C APIs each in their own dialect."
>
	<section>
		<h2>Which strings squill rewrites</h2>
		<p>
			Raw string literals (<code>R"(&hellip;)"</code>, with or without a
			delimiter like <code>R"sql(&hellip;)sql"</code>), whether written on one
			line or several. A query that outgrows its line is laid out between the
			delimiters, on lines of its own. Plain strings are left exactly as written
			&mdash; to have squill format a query, write it as a raw string.
		</p>
		<p>
			The built-in <code>c++</code> grammar&rsquo;s default query knows which
			database each C API talks to, so sqlite3&rsquo;s calls format as SQLite
			and libpq&rsquo;s as Postgres, whatever the configured dialect.
		</p>
	</section>

